{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pulls/2086","id":4891655287,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSaSRXM8AAAABI5C8dw","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pull/2086","diff_url":"https://github.com/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pull/2086.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pull/2086.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/issues/2086","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pulls/2086/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pulls/2086/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/issues/2086/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathanong/no-mistakes/statuses/099cfed26a23050aee6e9e8427af4de9b7eab4ef","number":2086,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"perf(graph): reuse cached parameter annotation values","user":{"login":"jonathanong","id":643505,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MzUwNQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/643505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathanong","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathanong/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nStore the annotated parameter value in the existing request-scoped parameter cache after runtime agreement and contextual fallback. Ready hits reuse that value instead of rebuilding its annotation provenance.\n\n## Impact\n\nEffects and call-graph queries retain the same prepared resolver scope and report fields. No new cache or persisted state is added. The existing cache retains a larger annotated payload; cold construction and peak RSS must earn the repeated-read benefit before this draft is ready.\n\n## Related issues\n\n- Closes #2076 — Reuses prepared annotation values through the existing parameter cache and adds ownership, work-count, and compiled API regressions.\n\n## Details\n\nThe saved regression changes 24 annotation computations for 24 reads into one per existing cache key and generation. Tests cover separate parameters/scopes, unresolved and cyclic types, untyped/recursive reads, generation clears, and independent prepared catalogs.\n\nLocal focused validation passed 672 graph/typed-rule tests. Parameters have 100% line/function/region coverage; provenance exceeds 99%. Six compiled CJS/ESM/prepared API tests passed on release candidate `5235102fb`, based on main `4aea22103`. Main `5decc19aa` is now integrated at `0076d3d70`; all 18 feature files are unchanged, and normal push hooks including all-target/all-feature Clippy passed on that integrated source.\n\nCurrent-source native validation, required CI/global98 coverage, and matched cold/consuming/non-consuming CPU, wall, and peak-RSS measurements remain pending. The artifacts based on `4aea22103` are historical evidence, not a current-main performance gate. Keep this PR a draft until the remaining gates pass.\n\nWorkspace setup: Dedicated linked worktree based on main 5decc19aa, carrying the reviewed feature commit 5235102fb and an ordinary main merge.\nAgent: Codex (GPT-6) session nm2076-parameter-annotation-cache\nDevice: jong@jong-z890-eagle-wifi7-plus\nWorktree: no-mistakes-2076-publish\n\n<details>\n<summary>Shepherd Journal</summary>\n\n- Published draft at `0076d3d7068ca2bc51d6957e25ee3c288a2e3415` with all normal hooks passing, including all-target/all-feature Clippy. The saved regression records 24 annotation evaluations before caching and 1 afterward; 672 focused graph/typed-rule tests pass, with 100% parameter-path coverage and >99% provenance coverage. Six compiled CJS/ESM/prepared API tests passed on the retained historical release candidate `5235102fb` / baseline source `4aea22103`. Main `5decc19aa` is integrated with all 18 feature files byte-identical, but its full native validation, exact-head CI/global98 coverage, and matched cold/consuming/non-consuming CPU/wall/RSS gates remain pending. The obsolete owned baseline build was cancelled after main changed; no timing samples or performance PASS exist. Keep DRAFT; do not start readiness/merge iteration before the remaining gates are genuinely satisfied.\n- Published head 0076d3d7068ca2bc51d6957e25ee3c288a2e3415 passed Test CI 38936559882 and all four Codecov contexts. Independent raw TOTAL readback: 98.4958% regions, 99.3870% functions, 99.3535% lines, with all configured 98% floors unchanged. This validates the published main5de integration, not the prospective c896 integration. Current native/performance gates remain pending and this PR remains draft. Evidence: /tmp/nm2076-ci-after-prospective-start/actual-exact-head-global98-review.json.\n</details>","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T17:01:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T17:47:59Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b59424d24b66af7f0e202e8143ed9806f15d2d7d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"jonathanong:fix/2076-parameter-annotation-cache","ref":"fix/2076-parameter-annotation-cache","repo":{"id":1235521884,"node_id":"R_kgDOSaSRXA","name":"no-mistakes","full_name":"jonathanong/no-mistakes","owner":{"login":"j